comments.body:
@participant5 sound plausible, and I like your implementation choice keeping it in the traefik domain, so no external dependencies.

Okay, what about a little logic where you can either use a full cycle OR the `Syn, Syn/Ack, Rst` approach, does that make sense? 
So a user would have the option to choose the data in and out as a valid check, custom protocol, legacy server OR the performance oriented way.

@participant7 I opted for a separate healthcheck to follow the existing pattern (up to 3.x), as most features under the TCP stack had their own copy implementation from its regular http side. Also note that the PR was made with the intention of going in incremental steps, from the ground up, as I was not in a hurry and wanted to move it forward with iterative reviews from the maintainers, which is always nice because it triggers exactly this kind of design / implementation discussions and decisions must be taken along the way. 

It would be easier to just hack my way into the code and have a working implementation (which I did in a private branch) but I believe this iterative approach pays out in the long run.

@rtribotte if the decision is made to go with a common healthcheck package for both http and tcp I can definitely refactor the branch to accomodate that, I could also find some time for a live session to coordinate what is the direction and nail down any implementation details. I intentionally did not touch the PR any further while following the discussions here.
